  "body": "This reminds me a bit of #69640 for unclaimed bindings on `ng-template`, and #70808 / #71844 for class bindings on `ng-container`. In #70808, which mentioned:\n\n> Those are never applied and we should throw at compiler time.\n\nThe `ng-content` part was also discussed in #24259 and #68715, where it was [mentioned](https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/68715#issuecomment-4446935264):\n\n> Is this maybe more appropriate as a template diagnostic or eslint? Breaking compilation on something entirely innocuous seems maybe incorrect.\n\nI see this proposal covers more cases, but I think some of these checks could also be handled by ESLint. \n\nSo I think maybe we can comment in that issue or PR ",
