  "created_at": "2026-11-08T20:50:04Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-08T20:50:04Z",
  "body": "> Fyi, About `ng-template` I was testing things on [#71887](https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/71887) and it raised a behavior that was implemented by [#53457](https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/53457).\n\nThanks for flagging it. #71882 keeps that behavior. On an explicit `<ng-template>`, it treats `[attr.x]`, `[class.x]`, and `[style.x]` as property bindings named `x`, as the compiler has done since #53457 ([`compilesToProperty`](https://github.com/Flarette/angular/blob/0747cac2983d4a4a9bbb69526e5693680a279f3e/packages/compiler/src/typecheck/ops/ignored_bindings.ts#L147-L162)). A directive input named `x` claims them, so NG8031 only reports the ones nothing claims.\n\nCovered in [`ignored_bindings_spec.ts`](https://github.com/Flarette/angular/blob/0747cac2983d4a4a9bbb69526e5693680a279f3e/packages/compiler-cli/test/ngtsc/ignored_bindings_spec.ts#L285-L299):\n- `should not report a class binding on ng-template` (`p-input-dir [class.p]`)\n- `should not report a style binding on ng-template` (`p-input-dir [style.p]`)\n- `should not report an attribute binding on ng-template` (`p-input-dir [attr.p]`)\n- `should report a class binding on ng-template` and `should report an attribute binding on ng-template` (no directive claims them)\n\nThe `ng_template_bindings` compliance test from #53457 stays as it is.\n\nIs this the behavior you ran into on #71887, or was it something else?",
  "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
